{"id":"60b7ba34-a24b-41c9-a60f-5db844ee835a","recipient":"4f46c5d7-aaf4-4f5d-a8ca-eac2a671a001","sender":"e364abe0-bce1-41d9-b227-52fc0551b34c","priority":"MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH","timestamp":"2026-09-01T06:52:49.770333600Z","renderDetails":{"messageTitle":"Message from Map Renderer 5 (coder)"},"content":"Here is the Python script to render frames 361 to 450 of the world map animation for a flight from Washington D.C. to New Delhi. The script uses matplotlib, cartopy, and pyproj to draw a great circle path and animate the progress.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport cartopy.crs as ccrs\nimport cartopy.feature as cfeature\n\ndef render_frames(start_frame, end_frame, total_frames=900):\n    # Washington D.C. and New Delhi coordinates\n    lon1, lat1 = -77.0369, 38.9072\n    lon2, lat2 = 77.2090, 28.6139\n\n    for frame in range(start_frame, end_frame + 1):\n        fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n        ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 1, 1, projection=ccrs.Robinson())\n        ax.set_global()\n        \n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.LAND, facecolor='lightgray')\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.OCEAN, facecolor='lightblue')\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.COASTLINE, linewidth=0.5)\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.BORDERS, linewidth=0.5, linestyle=':')\n        \n        # Plot the entire path lightly\n        ax.plot([lon1, lon2], [lat1, lat2], transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=1)\n        \n        progress = frame / total_frames\n        \n        try:\n            import pyproj\n            g = pyproj.Geod(ellps='WGS84')\n            lonlats = g.npts(lon1, lat1, lon2, lat2, total_frames)\n            current_lon, current_lat = lonlats[frame-1]\n            path_lons = [lon1] + [p[0] for p in lonlats[:frame]]\n            path_lats = [lat1] + [p[1] for p in lonlats[:frame]]\n        except ImportError:\n            current_lon = lon1 + (lon2 - lon1) * progress\n            current_lat = lat1 + (lat2 - lat1) * progress\n            path_lons = np.linspace(lon1, current_lon, frame)\n            path_lats = np.linspace(lat1, current_lat, frame)\n\n        ax.plot(path_lons, path_lats, transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), color='red', linewidth=2)\n        ax.plot(current_lon, current_lat, transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), marker='o', color='blue', markersize=6)\n        \n        ax.text(lon1 - 5, lat1 - 5, 'Washington D.C.', transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), fontsize=8)\n        ax.text(lon2 + 5, lat2 + 5, 'New Delhi', transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), fontsize=8)\n        \n        plt.title(f\"Flight Animation - Frame {frame:04d}\")\n        \n        filename = f\"frame_{frame:04d}.png\"\n        plt.savefig(filename, dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n        plt.close(fig)\n        print(f\"Saved {filename}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    render_frames(361, 450)\n```","sourceMetadata":{"tool":{"conversationId":"e364abe0-bce1-41d9-b227-52fc0551b34c","stepIndex":3,"toolCall":{"id":"call_3639251","name":"send_message","argumentsJson":"{\"Message\":\"Here is the Python script to render frames 361 to 450 of the world map animation for a flight from Washington D.C. to New Delhi. The script uses matplotlib, cartopy, and pyproj to draw a great circle path and animate the progress.\\n\\n```python\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nimport cartopy.crs as ccrs\\nimport cartopy.feature as cfeature\\n\\ndef render_frames(start_frame, end_frame, total_frames=900):\\n    # Washington D.C. and New Delhi coordinates\\n    lon1, lat1 = -77.0369, 38.9072\\n    lon2, lat2 = 77.2090, 28.6139\\n\\n    for frame in range(start_frame, end_frame + 1):\\n        fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\\n        ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 1, 1, projection=ccrs.Robinson())\\n        ax.set_global()\\n        \\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.LAND, facecolor='lightgray')\\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.OCEAN, facecolor='lightblue')\\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.COASTLINE, linewidth=0.5)\\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.BORDERS, linewidth=0.5, linestyle=':')\\n        \\n        # Plot the entire path lightly\\n        ax.plot([lon1, lon2], [lat1, lat2], transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=1)\\n        \\n        progress = frame / total_frames\\n        \\n        try:\\n            import pyproj\\n            g = pyproj.Geod(ellps='WGS84')\\n            lonlats = g.npts(lon1, lat1, lon2, lat2, total_frames)\\n            current_lon, current_lat = lonlats[frame-1]\\n            path_lons = [lon1] + [p[0] for p in lonlats[:frame]]\\n            path_lats = [lat1] + [p[1] for p in lonlats[:frame]]\\n        except ImportError:\\n            current_lon = lon1 + (lon2 - lon1) * progress\\n            current_lat = lat1 + (lat2 - lat1) * progress\\n            path_lons = np.linspace(lon1, current_lon, frame)\\n            path_lats = np.linspace(lat1, current_lat, frame)\\n\\n        ax.plot(path_lons, path_lats, transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), color='red', linewidth=2)\\n        ax.plot(current_lon, current_lat, transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), marker='o', color='blue', markersize=6)\\n        \\n        ax.text(lon1 - 5, lat1 - 5, 'Washington D.C.', transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), fontsize=8)\\n        ax.text(lon2 + 5, lat2 + 5, 'New Delhi', transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), fontsize=8)\\n        \\n        plt.title(f\\\"Flight Animation - Frame {frame:04d}\\\")\\n        \\n        filename = f\\\"frame_{frame:04d}.png\\\"\\n        plt.savefig(filename, dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\\n        plt.close(fig)\\n        print(f\\\"Saved {filename}\\\")\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    render_frames(361, 450)\\n```\",\"Recipient\":\"4f46c5d7-aaf4-4f5d-a8ca-eac2a671a001\",\"toolAction\":\"Sending python code\",\"toolSummary\":\"Python code for animation\"}","thinkingSignature":""}}}}